From 42ae09b3602c722d3b0ec771c4915507b2d69daf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: its-rosetta <267385802+its-rosetta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:49:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(provider-codex): name the rejected request's method,
 code, and kind

A provider rejection used to surface as the constant "codex app-server
rejected the request", so a subscription-router capacity failure was
indistinguishable from any other error. The remote error is now a closed,
declaratively classified kind (remote-error.ts) whose message carries the
request method, the numeric JSON-RPC code, and an authored summary for
recognized kinds. The response body is read once to choose the kind and is
never retained, preserving the provider-admission redaction boundary.

Subscription-router rejections (no capacity, ceilings reached, not
connected, child exited) are recognized by their router-owned JSON-RPC codes.
Malformed-response and timeout errors also name the method.
